.TH TESSERA-CONTROLLER-COMMAND 8 "" "Tessera" "System administration"
.SH NAME
tessera-controller-command \- Tessera system helper
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
tessera-controller-command -n COMMAND [ARGUMENT ...]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Bounded unprivileged adapter used by the compatibility runtime. Accepts only its flow replacement, reload and local control forms. It never grants privileges; use tesseractl for operator commands.
.PP
A flow report that names flows replaces the daemon's controller flow set. An empty report is applied only if the runtime has already applied a report in its current systemd invocation, so the empty report the runtime makes when it starts does not remove flows stored with tesseractl flows set. The invocation that last applied a report is kept in /var/lib/tessera-controller/flows-run.
.SH SEE ALSO
tesserad(8), tesseractl(1)
